Feature: Extract Product Size and Update Product Description with Timestamp

  Background:
    Given a database table named "purgo_playground.product_desc" with columns:
      | product_id        | product_description                                                 | product_size           | dimension_1 | dimension_2 | dimension_3 |
    And a target table named "purgo_playground.product_desc" for storing processed records
    And a timestamp column "timestemp" defined with the format "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS"

  Scenario Outline: Extract and Validate Product Size From Product Description
    Given a product record with product_id "<product_id>" and product_description "<product_description>"
    When the system extracts the product size using the description
    Then the extracted product size should be "<expected_size>"
    And a validation message should confirm "Valid size extracted"
    And the system updates the table with the new "timestemp"

    Examples:
      | product_id                           | product_description                                                                                   | expected_size         |
      | YRDMT-6061-T6511-TB-3.7500-.3750-23.7000 | ALUM EXTRUDED ROUND TUBE - BAR - 1-Aluminum Bar - 6061-T6511-TB - 6061-T6511-TB-3.7500-.3750-23.7000 | 3.7500-.3750-23.7000 |

  Scenario: Extraction Failure and Fallback to Product ID
    Given a product record with product_id "YRDMT-7075-T73-TB-2.8750" and product_description "ALUMINUM EXTRUDED TUBING - BAR - 1-Aluminum Bar - 7075-T73-TB - 7075-T73-TB-2.8750"
    When the system fails to extract the product size from the description
    Then the system should fall back to the product_id pattern for size extraction
    And the extracted product size should be "2.8750"
    And update the table with the new "timestemp"

  Scenario Outline: Validate Data Format and Handle Errors
    Given a product record with product_id "<product_id>" and product_description "<invalid_product_description>"
    When an invalid product description is encountered during size extraction
    Then the system should not produce a product size
    And an error message "Extraction failed due to invalid format" should be logged

    Examples:
      | product_id | invalid_product_description                                                 |
      | YRDMT-9999 | INVALID PRODUCT DESCRIPTION with no size info                               |

  Scenario Outline: Handle Missing Product Size and Populate with Product ID
    Given a product record with product_id "<product_id>" and product_description "<product_description>"
    When the system detects a missing product_size field
    Then it extracts size from the product_id
    And populate the product_size with "<expected_size>"
    And update the table with the new "timestemp"

    Examples:
      | product_id                           | product_description                                                | expected_size |
      | YRDMT-6061-T6511-TB-4.5000-1.0000-104.1550 | ALUM EXTRUDED ROUND                                               | 4.5000-1.0000-104.1550 |

  Scenario: Validate Integration with Existing Database Schema
    Given a table structure in "purgo_playground.product_desc" with existing columns and newly added "timestemp"
    When product_size is extracted from product_description successfully
    Then ensure seamless integration without data conflicts
    And ensure the new column adheres to schema constraints

  Scenario Outline: Invalid Product Description Handling
    Given a product record with an invalid product_description "<product_description>"
    When the system attempts to extract product_size
    Then it should log an error stating "Invalid format"
    And the product_size should remain empty

    Examples:
      | product_description      |
      | INVALID DESCRIPTION DATA |
